  "claim_boundary": "This Programme successor records current protected cross-repository OTP navigation state only. Forge remains authoritative for source identity and semantic/nonvacuity clearance, Solve for producer packets and handoff provenance, Cert for route registration, adjudication, disposition and output, and Programme only for cross-repository navigation. The six listed restricted qualification surfaces remain bounded qualifications and do not mark mathematical targets proved. OTP-A-SPHERE-PACKING is recorded only as adjudication_clear_protected_four_targets_only on a still-submitted route with cert_output null and no authority in this record to issue output or transition the route. OTP-H-GAPCVP, OTP-B1-BINARY-CODES and OTP-B2-SPHERICAL-CODES are recorded only at protected executable work-package state, with exact replay/evidence as the next boundary and no inferred route proposal, registration, adjudication or output authority. OTP-I-RAMSEY, OTP-G-QUANTUM-PARALLEL-REPETITION, OTP-D-NON-SOFIC and OTP-E-CONNES-RIGIDITY are recorded only as current-root Forge semantic/nonvacuity clearances; no Solve handoff or Cert authority is inferred. Historical Programme records are preserved byte-identically and are not rewritten. This record does not establish whole-document byte or semantic equivalence, compare proof bodies in full, broaden any restricted certificate, promote any mathematical target, transfer authority between families, create an aggregate OpenAI Ten Proofs route, adjudication, certificate or proof object, or authorize novelty, priority, publication, patentability, product or commercial claims."
